# Digital/Decimation Filter System

## Overview
A complete Verilog-based signal processing system that implements a multi-stage decimation filter chain for converting high-speed 1-bit sigma-delta modulated data into high-resolution digital signals. The system features a demodulator followed by a Cascaded Integrator-Comb (CIC) filter with additional downsampling stages.

## System Architecture

### Module Hierarchy
```
top (Complete Processing Chain)
├── demodulator (1-bit to 2-bit converter)
└── full_filter (Two-stage decimation)
    ├── cic_top (CIC Filter Core)
    │   ├── all_integrators (N-stage integration)
    │   │   └── integrator (Basic accumulator)
    │   ├── downsampler (Rate reduction)
    │   └── all_combs (N-stage differentiation)
    │       └── comb (Basic differentiator)
    └── downsampler_without_out_ready (Final decimation)
```

### Signal Flow
```
1-bit ADC Input → Demodulator → 2-bit Data → CIC Filter (R1) → Downsampler (R2) → 20-bit Output
    (4.096 MHz)           (4.096 MHz)        (4.096 MHz)        (8 kHz)             (2 kHz)
```

